        "original_id": "408d9c47-5845-5bdb-b20f-b3aab8afe614",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Black Velvet Gown, Harry Potter film series\n- People: Catherine Cookson, Janet McTeer, Geraldine Somerville, Bob Peck\n- Roles: Detective Sergeant Jane Penhaligon, Lily Potter\n- Events: 1995 BAFTA TV Award for Best Actress\n\nFacts:\n- The Black Velvet Gown is a 1991 TV film based on a novel by Catherine Cookson.\n- The Black Velvet Gown stars Janet McTeer, Geraldine Somerville, and Bob Peck.\n- Geraldine Margaret Agnew-Somerville was born on 19 May 1967 and is an Irish-born actress.\n- Geraldine Somerville played Detective Sergeant Jane Penhaligon in Cracker from 1993 to 1995.\n- Geraldine Somerville was nominated for the 1995 BAFTA TV Award for Best Actress for her role in Cracker.\n- Geraldine Somerville played Lily Potter in the Harry Potter film series.",
